{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head 7b5c0701883a4062691a14afe7dd7d0141b3b14b, judging artifact 5f28945fa078b5c25227d924fa73e0e3bc3ceab2.\n\nFour blocking findings.\n\n1. The executable walkthrough creates the merged artifact but discards its EventID, then supersedes the branch artifact with no causal basis naming the successor. The later audit still runs provenance on the retired branch artifact. Capture `MERGED_ARTIFACT=$(gs state ...)`, pass `--rests-on \"$MERGED_ARTIFACT\"` before the supersede target, and audit `$MERGED_ARTIFACT`. The target must remain the first basis; the successor is the additional basis. Prose saying “Superseded by the merge artifact” is not a durable pointer.\n\n2. The same missing-link rule appears in the reference table. Consolidating a narrow artifact into a wider live artifact must cite that wider artifact as an additional supersede basis. A rename must create or identify the destination artifact and cite it when retiring the old-path artifact. Bare supersession is correct only when there is genuinely no successor, such as deletion. First-basis authorization does not require throwing away the successor basis.\n\n3. The four cases are not exhaustive as written. The rename row says a rename opens a first artifact at the new path, but the destination can already have a live artifact. State the destination collision case and reuse/succeed that live path rather than publishing an assumed first artifact.\n\n4. Both changed pages knowingly keep anchors that contradict the guidance. merge.md rests on retired/stale artifact 7bf40860; end-to-end.md rests on comma-joined pseudo-path artifacts that the new text correctly says cannot participate in succession. These are not optional follow-ups for a head whose purpose is truthful merge guidance. Republish the affected behavior/docs artifacts at real stable paths, retire the broken predecessors with the authorized actors, and update frontmatter to the live replacements before re-review.\n\nThe content split between reference and how-to is otherwise sound, exact-string matching is explained clearly, the no-dot rationale is appropriate, and self-initiated-work wording matches current AGENTS.md. `go vet ./...` and `go test ./internal/docset -count=1` pass; the passing docset gate does not exercise successor causality, rename destination collisions, or current anchor quality.","body":{"head":"7b5c0701883a4062691a14afe7dd7d0141b3b14b","verdict":"changes-requested"}}